@page "/demo/variable-height/incident/net10"
@layout DemoLayout

<h1>Order sync incident</h1>

@* The same thread on .NET 10, measured: the jump is in Virtualize's own script, so it can't run on this
   .NET 11 site. The chart is the list's height after each scroll step, from the repro. *@
<Net10Recording Sdk="10.0.102" Request="scroll down 40 × 400px, measuring the list's height each time"
                Repro="virtualize-variable-height" Note="Measured with Playwright (probes/virtualize-variable-height-series.mjs).">
    <p class="chart-title">The list's height after each scroll step</p>
    <HeightChart Heights="Measured.Net10" />
    <p class="measured" data-measured>
        The list never changed, but its height swung between <b>33,057px</b> and <b>45,607px</b> as you scrolled.
        That's the scrollbar jumping. Then Expand all pushed the message being read <b>549px</b> down.
    </p>
</Net10Recording>
